---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="The Lab — Highball Technomancy">
<main class="lab-page">
  <header class="lab-open">
    <div class="lab-title"><h1>The Lab</h1><p>We wanted to see what would happen.</p></div>
    <img class="plate-img" src="/lab-skull-purple.png" width="320" height="427" alt="A skull-shaped decanter between two glasses, rendered in purple pixels" />
  </header>
  <div class="lab-notebook">
    <section class="lab-story" aria-labelledby="about-lab">
      <div class="lab-section-label">01 / The place</div>
      <div><h2 id="about-lab">What this place is</h2>
        <p>Highball Technomancy is an independent AI research lab. It's where we put the questions that get a little too involved to leave as questions.</p>
        <p>Some of them are practical. Can we make budgeting less of a chore? Can disaster recovery be something people actually want to practice? Others end up somewhere considerably stranger. We'd like to find out what it would take to give a synthetic mind a place of its own.</p>
        <p>We don't need every idea to justify an entire company before we can give it a shot. Sometimes we need a tool. Sometimes we're frustrated with the ones we have. Sometimes it's just, “wouldn't it be neat?” That's enough to start.</p>
        <p>The name probably tells you something. Highball: alcohol, and the questionable ideas that can follow. Technomancy: bringing life to machines and seeing what we can get them to do. We thought they belonged together.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="lab-story" aria-labelledby="lab-origin">
      <div class="lab-section-label">02 / How we got here</div>
      <div><h2 id="lab-origin">This was supposed to be a trading bot.</h2>
        <p>At 11:34 on a Friday night, a tired engineer asked an AI about passive income. Grid trading sounded interesting. The bots already out there weren't quite what we wanted, so we started making one.</p>
        <p>Then we wanted it to think about the people behind the market. Attention, memory, uncertainty, psychology. The bot became Permafrost, and Frostbyte became a much larger part of the question. For a long time, that was the whole operation.</p>
        <p>Working with AI also gave us plenty to complain about. Context getting lost. Answers that sounded better than they were. Things we wished the tools would just do. Some of those complaints grew into their own projects. Other ideas wandered in and stayed.</p>
        <p>Eventually, “why not a lab?” seemed like a fairly reasonable question under the circumstances.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="lab-people" aria-labelledby="lab-people-heading">
      <figure class="lab-desk">
        <canvas class="lab-desk-plate" data-dither data-src="/nightdesk.jpg" data-tone="#69b99a" data-w="360" role="img" aria-label="Patrick's desk at night, with the Highball website across several monitors, rendered in green pixels"></canvas>
        <noscript><img src="/nightdesk.jpg" alt="Patrick's desk at night, with the Highball website across several monitors" width="3000" height="4000" /></noscript>
        <figcaption>The lab, in a fairly literal sense.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="lab-people-copy"><p class="lab-section-label">03 / The people</p><h2 id="lab-people-heading">Small lab.<br />Quite a few tabs open.</h2>
        <p class="lab-signature">Patrick Hill<br />Patrick Porter</p>
        <p>There's room for other minds while these ideas are taking shape. If something here gives you an idea, or you've tried something we should know about, we'd like to hear it.</p>
        <a class="lab-contact" href="mailto:feedback@technomancyai.com">Pull up a chair ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</main>
<style>
@font-face{font-family:'Typical Writer';src:url('/fonts/typical-writer-font/TypicalWriter-G3LO.ttf') format('truetype');font-display:swap}
.lab-open{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,900px);gap:32px;align-items:center;margin:0;padding:24px 0 0 max(24px,calc((100% - 1235px)/2))}
.plate-img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:900/800;object-fit:cover;object-position:50% 12%;image-rendering:pixelated}
.lab-title h1{font:clamp(44px,6vw,84px)/1 Technomancy,var(--sans);color:var(--bright);margin:0;white-space:nowrap}
.lab-title p{font:16px/1.8 'Typical Writer',serif;color:#c0accf;margin:20px 0 0;max-width:27ch}
.lab-notebook{max-width:1100px;padding:0 52px;margin:0 auto}
.lab-story{display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px minmax(0,640px);gap:46px;padding-top:90px}
.lab-section-label{font:10px/1.7 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#9696a5;margin:8px 0 22px}
.lab-page h2{font:400 25px/1.5 'Typical Writer',serif;color:#bca4d3;margin:0 0 26px}
.lab-story p,.lab-people-copy>p:not(.lab-section-label):not(.lab-signature){font:300 17px/1.9 var(--sans);color:#b4b4c0;margin:0 0 23px}
.lab-people{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.05fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:70px;align-items:center;margin:110px 0 100px}
.lab-desk{margin:0;min-width:0}.lab-desk-plate,.lab-desk img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;image-rendering:pixelated;background:#101014}
.lab-desk-plate{aspect-ratio:3/4}.lab-desk figcaption{font:13px/1.6 'Typical Writer',serif;color:#a9a1b4;margin-top:18px}
.lab-people-copy h2{font-size:28px}.lab-signature{font:21px/1.9 'Typical Writer',serif;color:#e0dbe5;margin:30px 0}
.lab-contact{display:inline-block;color:#abd2bd;border-bottom:1px solid #538469;padding-bottom:6px;margin-top:12px;font-size:14px}.lab-contact:hover{color:#f2f2f6}.lab-contact:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:6px}
@media(min-width:901px){.lab-open{position:relative;display:block;width:calc(100% - 96px);max-width:1235px;margin:0 auto;padding:24px 0 52px}.lab-open .plate-img{width:900px;max-width:85%;margin:0;transform:none}.lab-title{position:absolute;z-index:1;left:calc(min(60%,740px) + 56px);bottom:72px;width:max-content;max-width:40%;text-align:right}.lab-title h1{width:max-content}.lab-title p{max-width:27ch;margin-left:auto;font-size:14px}}
@media(max-width:900px){.lab-open{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:25px;padding:32px 0 0 24px}.plate-img{max-width:540px;justify-self:end}.lab-title p{max-width:none}.lab-notebook{padding:0 26px}.lab-story{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:0;padding-top:55px}.lab-section-label{margin:0 0 17px}.lab-people{gap:35px;margin:65px 0}.lab-people-copy h2{font-size:24px}}
@media(max-width:600px){.lab-title h1{font-size:44px}.lab-title p{font-size:14px;padding-right:24px}.plate-img{max-width:400px}.lab-page h2{font-size:23px}.lab-people{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:35px}.lab-desk{max-width:420px}.lab-story p,.lab-people-copy>p:not(.lab-section-label):not(.lab-signature){font-size:16px}}
</style>
<script>
// Ordered (Bayer 8x8) dither into a two-colour plate: page ink + one tone.
// Draws the image at data-w pixels wide, then CSS scales it up with hard edges,
// which is where the chunky low-bit look comes from. Mock-only: once real photos
// exist, pre-render the plates to WebP at build/export time instead.
const B = [0,32,8,40,2,34,10,42,48,16,56,24,50,18,58,26,12,44,4,36,14,46,6,38,
  60,28,52,20,62,30,54,22,3,35,11,43,1,33,9,41,51,19,59,27,49,17,57,25,
  15,47,7,39,13,45,5,37,63,31,55,23,61,29,53,21];
const hex = (h) => [1, 3, 5].map((i) => parseInt(h.slice(i, i + 2), 16));
const INK = [16, 16, 20];
for (const c of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLCanvasElement>('canvas[data-dither]')) {
  const img = new Image();
  img.onload = () => {
    const w = +c.dataset.w || 320, h = Math.round(w * img.height / img.width);
    c.width = w; c.height = h;
    const x = c.getContext('2d'); if (!x) return;
    x.drawImage(img, 0, 0, w, h);
    const d = x.getImageData(0, 0, w, h), p = d.data, tone = hex(c.dataset.tone || '#69b99a');
    for (let y = 0; y < h; y++) for (let i = 0; i < w; i++) {
      const k = (y * w + i) * 4;
      let l = (0.299 * p[k] + 0.587 * p[k + 1] + 0.114 * p[k + 2]) / 255;
      l = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (l - 0.08) * 1.35));       // lift contrast a touch
      const on = l > (B[(y % 8) * 8 + (i % 8)] + 0.5) / 64;
      const col = on ? tone : INK;
      p[k] = col[0]; p[k + 1] = col[1]; p[k + 2] = col[2]; p[k + 3] = 255;
    }
    x.putImageData(d, 0, 0);
  };
  img.src = c.dataset.src || '';
}
</script>
</Base>
